    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hey there.\r\n\r\nWondering if this is a fixable issue with mini.comments. \r\n\r\nI work on a C codebase which uses the '/* */' comment syntax. \r\n\r\nIt appears that `mini.comment` can create comments correctly, but once the comment is inserted, it doesn't understand how to uncomment it, and instead adds another comment in the `//` comment syntax. \r\n\r\nI've uploaded a screencap to explain. \r\n\r\nI read thru the help but nothing stood out to me on how to fix this. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5784744d-94cd-4666-b74d-b137758a24ad\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hey there.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Wondering if this is a fixable issue with mini.comments.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I work on a C codebase which uses the '/* */' comment syntax.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It appears that <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.comment</code> can create comments correctly, but once the comment is inserted, it doesn't understand how to uncomment it, and instead adds another comment in the <code class=\"notranslate\">//</code> comment syntax.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've uploaded a screencap to explain.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I read thru the help but nothing stood out to me on how to fix this.</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">Screen.Recording.2024-12-06.at.8.15.09.AM.mov</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/5642902/393260137-5784744d-94cd-4666-b74d-b137758a24ad.mov?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..2TKuA_wR5OxkSSrx-UzoG_guTjV1_2n3HBU18I_DK9M\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/5642902/393260137-5784744d-94cd-4666-b74d-b137758a24ad.mov?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..2TKuA_wR5OxkSSrx-UzoG_guTjV1_2n3HBU18I_DK9M\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n",
    "bodyText": "Hey there.\nWondering if this is a fixable issue with mini.comments.\nI work on a C codebase which uses the '/* */' comment syntax.\nIt appears that mini.comment can create comments correctly, but once the comment is inserted, it doesn't understand how to uncomment it, and instead adds another comment in the // comment syntax.\nI've uploaded a screencap to explain.\nI read thru the help but nothing stood out to me on how to fix this.\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    Screen.Recording.2024-12-06.at.8.15.09.AM.mov",
